    "description": "The Arsenal Season Review 2006 - 2007 ('The Young Guns') DVD features all the best action from the Arsenal Football Club's first historic season at Emirates Stadium on Ashburton Grove. This season witnessed Arsene Wenger build what is potentially the most exciting team in the Club's history and, in a rollercoaster campaign, the Gunners had many highlights. Among these were: a premiership double over Manchester United; a thrilling Carling Cup run that saw Liverpool hit for a six; a full strength Spurs overcome by the Arsenal Young Guns; plus many great goals that have confirmed Arsenal as one of the most entertaining sides in the country. The Arsenal Season Review 2006-2007 also includes: exclusive interviews with the manager and many of the team's leading players; a profile of the all-conquering Women's team who won the UEFA Cup Final; plus a complete list of Club records and landmarks for the season.",
